  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 354 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nA weak cold front moves southeast out of the Blackhills \nregion and progresses into the northwest Sandhills by Sunday \nmorning. This will cool temperatures into the 70s Sunday. The \nfront will slowly move southeast and will see one more day of \nabove normal temperatures across most of the forecast area with \nhighs in the 80s, with the exception of northwest Sandhills. The\nfront stalls out Monday across the southern Sandhills , keeping\none more day 80s across far southwest Nebraska.\n\nWill see cooler temperatures continue to progress Tuesday and \nWednesday as the cool air mass pushes southeast into the region\nwith highs in the 50s and 60s. There will also be chances for \nprecipitation with increase moisture and weak disturbances on \nTuesday night through early Thursday. Will need to continue to \nmonitor overnight lows Friday night into Saturday as lows will \nbe in the low to mid 30s across the northern Sandhills, if \ncooler trend continues with later forecast runs, frost/freeze \nheadlines may be needed.",
